From 7e1e87d80e3c8e3a9fa8764a34431857e50c1ca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ankit <akitsini2004@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:42:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix invisible search input, silent gap at record/resume, and
 replace/preview snap-back

1. Library search input: deterministic layout (explicit-width container,
   minWidth:0 + full-height input), visible caret (cursorColor) and
   selection color, brighter placeholder, subtle field border. autoFocus
   removed - the staggered retry effect drives focus so the field can
   never be focused before it is sized.

2. Silent gap at record start / resume: the native engine now keeps a
   warm (pre-opened, stopped) AudioRecord across pause/resume and between
   takes (prepareRecorder/dropWarmRecorder bridge methods). record() reuses
   it, so the 200-500 ms AudioRecord setup no longer eats the head of the
   segment. The warm mic is dropped when the app backgrounds or the
   session closes, so it never blocks other apps.

3. Playhead running ahead / snapping back: the JS transition freeze now
   stays on until the FIRST hardware meter for the target mode arrives
   (gated on the meter's recording flag so stale meters from the other
   mode are ignored). That meter re-anchors the clock to the true
   position, so the UI starts moving in step with the audio instead of
   ahead of it, and the 80 ms drift snap can no longer yank the playhead
   backwards after a switch. A 1.5 s guard releases the freeze if no
   meter ever arrives; IDLE/not-running snapshots release it immediately.
